  "text": "1. He got gradually ____ in the case, though he didn't intend to originally.\nA) connected  B) related\nC) interfered  D) involved\n2. He suddenly called my name on the street, but I could not ____ where I had met him before.\nA) remind  B) recall\nC) record  D) reclaim\n3. We are going to be very busy. There is a large ____ of work for us to do.\nA) amount  B) number\nC) lot  D) deal\n4. The insurance company will pay for the furniture ____ by fire.\nA) stolen  B) lost\nC) damaged  D) diminished\n5. The ____ of his laboratory took time and money.\nA) endurance  B) equipment\nC) efficiency  D) essence\n6. A new telescope that may reveal the new ____ has been set up.\nA) universe  B) sky\nC) orbit  D) space\n7. — Will you go to the movies with us tonight? — I'm sorry, I have not made up my ____ yet.\nA) heart  B) brain\nC) head  D) mind\n8. I put the medicine bottle on the high shelf in order to ____ children ____ reaching it.\nA) prevent … from  B) stop … from\nC) forbid … to  D) prohibit … to\n9. It was his pride that ____ in his failure in the final exam.\nA) led  B) resulted\nC) caused  D) gave\n10. His political ideas were too ____ to get support from ordinary people.\nA) competent  B) complex\nC) complimentary  D) confident\n11. Scientists have done ____ research to reveal the effects of cigarette smoking.\nA) much  B) many\nC) numerous  D) few\n12. Did you attend the party which ____ place in our department yesterday?\nA) was taken  B) gave\nC) took  D) was given\n13. This district has enormous ____ for economic development, but a great deal of money is needed.\nA) possibility  B) process\nC) sensibility  D) potential\n14. Although he has given us ____ information on that matter, we still can't come to a conclusion.\nA) many  B) an\nC) much  D) little",
