  "text": "15. I don't know why, but he has actually given us no ____ to our proposal.\nA) reflection  B) reaction\nC) relation  D) action\n16. Considerable excitement was ____ on the planet of Venus this week.\nA) involved  B) aroused\nC) arranged  D) exposed\n17. They were working at the technical ____ of a supersonic aircraft during my first visit.\nA) observation  B) motivation\nC) performance  D) feasibility\n18. As we passed through the town, two policemen ____ us to stop.\nA) signed  B) sighed\nC) signaled  D) sighted\n19. A planet's ____ is the layer of air or other gases around it.\nA) environment  B) atmosphere\nC) surrounding  D) circumstance\n20. The patients go out of their wards for some fresh ____ every afternoon.\nA) air  B) gas\nC) carbon  D) moisture\n21. The chemistry teacher asked the pupils what water was ____ of.\nA) consisted  B) combined\nC) converted  D) composed\n22. The plane crashed into the sea but over half of the passengers ____.\nA) lived  B) survived\nC) consolidated  D) contracted\n23. ____, the book was published as a series of magazine articles.\nA) Originally  B) Briefly\nC) Publicly  D) Occasionally\n24. He saved the child at the ____ of his life.\nA) danger  B) risk\nC) hazard  D) rate\n25. The helicopter hovered ____ the spot where the lost man had been last seen.\nA) under  B) on\nC) in  D) over\n26. He must be very nervous when speaking. Did you ____ that his hand was shaking.\nA) mind  B) attention\nC) watch  D) notice\n27. I remember that I ____ the Party before my graduation from the university.\nA) took  B) joined\nC) attended  D) occupied\n28. Mary doesn't want to go into the sea. She would rather lie on the ____.\nA) beach  B) coast\nC) bank  D) shore\n29. He was such a ____ young man that many girls liked him.\nA) pretty  B) beautiful\nC) handsome  D) wonderful\n30. Peter has two brothers. One of them is a teacher, ____ is a driver.\nA) another  B) the other\nC) other  D) each other\n31. Not until late at night did the boat ____ into the harbor.\nA) drive  B) drag\nC) pull  D) enter\n32. Stunned by what had happened, the old man stood ____ to the spot.\nA) tied  B) roped\nC) fastened  D) rooted\n33. I can't tell how old he is, for the sad and complex expression on his face ____ his age.\nA) masks  B) reveals\nC) shows  D) prevents",
