  "label": "选择题强化训练（二） 第 72–88 题",
  "text": "72. The candlelight at our dinner table was ____, but very romantic.\nA) little  B) small\nC) slim  D) faint\n73. Several days passed before they came up with a satisfactory solution ____ the problem.\nA) to  B) for\nC) with  D) at\n74. The American does not ____ the argument but watches the other guests.\nA) take part  B) join in\nC) attend to  D) run into\n75. Mrs. David wrote the article soon after she returned ____.\nA) to abroad  B) in abroad\nC) from abroad  D) at abroad\n76. There are in China over fifty nationalities (民族) ____ the Hans.\nA) except  B) except for\nC) beside  D) besides\n77. The windows were never opened ____ air the room for a few minutes in the morning.\nA) except for  B) except to\nC) except in  D) except with\n78. Mrs. Brown asked me to go to her daughter's concert and I ____ her invitation.\nA) accepted  B) received\nC) offered  D) gave\n79. The telephone, which was ____ by Bell in 1876, was a great improvement on the telegraph.\nA) discovered  B) found\nC) invented  D) made\n80. In spite of the hard winter, the roses in our garden are still ____.\nA) alive  B) alike\nC) astir  D) awake\n81. The values of American teenagers often differ ____ those of their parents.\nA) with  B) from\nC) between  D) for\n82. Manufacturing companies spend millions of pounds trying to convince customers that their products are superior ____ those of other companies.\nA) than  B) with\nC) to  D) from\n83. I applied for a job as a computer programmer in a local company, but was ____.\nA) offered  B) given\nC) agreed  D) rejected\n84. It was through his uncle's influence that Philip ____ his position with the biggest oil company.\nA) appointed  B) obtained\nC) resented  D) threatened\n85. The two criminals lived in ____ fear of being discovered.\nA) far-reaching  B) hard-working\nC) never-ending  D) easy-going\n86. A man of humble ____, Lincoln eventually became President of the United States through his own efforts.\nA) origin  B) source\nC) home  D) family\n87. Many species of animals which once lived on earth are no longer ____.\nA) in vain  B) in advance\nC) in addition  D) in existence\n88. ____ the advice of his doctor, Mr. Park had his eye operated on right after he retired last week.\nA) Acting on  B) Depending on\nC) Relying on  D) Taking on",
